WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.919
After two years and more than 100 videos.

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:04.379
Thanks to you guys.

00:00:04.379 --> 00:00:08.091
I was able to finally quit my job
and start my own architecture business.

00:00:08.591 --> 00:00:13.722
I met my dream client and I'm working on
some really cool projects,

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:17.767
but when I thought everything was going
perfectly fine,

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:20.687
the universe threw me a curveball .

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:30.947
It feels a little bit steeper than I thought it was gonna be.

00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:53.845
This is the site right here

00:00:53.845 --> 00:00:58.058
from about that pole
to probably somewhere over there.

00:00:58.933 --> 00:01:03.188
And it's one of those areas
with no sidewalks and nowhere

00:01:03.188 --> 00:01:07.025
to park your car because people
don't want you to come here.

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:10.070
And yesterday, actually, when I came here

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:13.698
with the client,
we parked our car right here.

00:01:13.698 --> 00:01:17.118
The neighbor came out
and told us to move our car

00:01:17.118 --> 00:01:18.787
in like 10 minutes.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.670
So I meet this Rhino model
before I came here

00:01:28.379 --> 00:01:31.299
based off of a survey
that was done in 2006.

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:34.594
I'm standing right over here.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:38.223
There is a slightly less steep
slope over there.

00:01:38.473 --> 00:01:42.102
So will enter into the site from that way.

00:01:42.727 --> 00:01:45.688
Good thing I brought my boots.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.909
There's a lot more trees than I expected.

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.161
So the site ends all the way up there.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.372
So we're not even close yet.

00:02:02.372 --> 00:02:04.415
So let's continue.

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:06.793
Whoa!

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:14.467
this over here is the protected oak tree.

00:02:14.676 --> 00:02:17.011
I think it's going to be really nice
to design around it.

00:02:17.262 --> 00:02:19.889
I stayed in a house
in Italy over the summer one time,

00:02:19.931 --> 00:02:23.601
and it was right
next to this massive oak tree.

00:02:24.227 --> 00:02:27.564
And it was just so beautiful
when you open the windows,

00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:30.817
you hear silence

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:33.820
and you hear the rustling of the leaves.

00:02:34.904 --> 00:02:37.949
And when you wake up early,
you can actually hear

00:02:37.949 --> 00:02:40.243
the birds wake up with you.

00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:43.746
So yeah, I'll just show you where

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:46.749
on the site we are right now.

00:02:46.749 --> 00:02:48.793
So we are right here.

00:02:49.085 --> 00:02:51.254
And that's the road just over.

00:02:51.713 --> 00:02:54.674
This entire thing is the site.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:59.512
As you can see, it's so steep over here.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.933
And it would have been impossible
for us to walk up this path,

00:03:04.559 --> 00:03:07.854
this entire area is very,
very steep as well.

00:03:08.229 --> 00:03:11.441
And there's just a lot of trees around.

00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:15.653
But I don't think I'm going to try
to even get up there.

00:03:16.404 --> 00:03:18.865
So we're facing east a bit

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:23.953
northeast,

00:03:23.953 --> 00:03:27.123
and because it's in a slightly hilly area,

00:03:28.082 --> 00:03:31.461
I think it
probably has its own little microclimate.

00:03:31.461 --> 00:03:36.966
But apparently it gets really,
really hot here because the Oakland Hills

00:03:37.091 --> 00:03:41.679
blocks a lot of the fog and the cool
air from coming down this area.

00:03:42.138 --> 00:03:45.892
So super hot and a little bit more
wet in the winters.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:52.065
I want to show you that massive
bird's nest.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:55.360
Here is the highlight
of my architectural experience right here.

00:03:56.319 --> 00:04:00.823
So I'm getting some footage of the site
with my Insta360 one camera

00:04:01.199 --> 00:04:06.037
and because it can grab
a 360 view of the site, it's

00:04:06.037 --> 00:04:11.960
so much more helpful than just being able
to grab photos or videos.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:12.210
There

00:04:13.378 --> 00:04:19.008
are four inches.

00:04:19.008 --> 00:04:23.554
I made it to the top of the site,
so the site actually goes in

00:04:24.514 --> 00:04:27.767
further up till about that point.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.687
But once you get there,
we have this house,

00:04:30.812 --> 00:04:34.482
so that's
probably not the most ideal place to site.

00:04:34.482 --> 00:04:35.984
Our building.

00:04:35.984 --> 00:04:39.821
There is a little bit of a flat area
right here

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.991
where the house could potentially sit on.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:47.829
And if these trees were cleared,
the view from here

00:04:48.579 --> 00:04:51.457
would be pretty,

00:04:51.499 --> 00:04:53.501
pretty nice.

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:56.129
The most important part of a site visit is

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:58.548
you need to feel the site.  

00:04:58.548 --> 00:04:59.882
And listen to the site.

00:04:59.882 --> 00:05:02.385
And become one with the site.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.351
Hem..are you okay?

00:05:10.727 --> 00:05:14.272
One of the things that I noticed
when I was there is how quickly got dark.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.733
We were there until about 4 p.m.

00:05:16.733 --> 00:05:21.612
and it was already starting to get dark
and that's because we have this

00:05:22.113 --> 00:05:25.533
really steep hill.

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:29.495
If so, that's me right there.

00:05:30.872 --> 00:05:36.169
And I mean, you can already see how steep
the slope is, right?

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:40.006
So that way is north, that's south.

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:43.301
And so if the sun

00:05:43.301 --> 00:05:48.014
is rising from the east, making its way

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:53.227
west, you can see over here

00:05:54.020 --> 00:06:01.027
there's a very big shadowed area.

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:04.906
And especially
as we get into the winter months,

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:07.700
when the sun starts getting lower,

00:06:08.326 --> 00:06:11.829
you get to even a bigger shadowed area.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:16.167
And I also tried doing a proper Sun study
and that's what I found here as well.

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:18.044
And I remember
when I was staying in Bolzano

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:22.048
in northern Italy,
which is also a very mountainous region,

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:26.803
that was one of the biggest complaints
there, that it got dark so fast.

00:06:27.261 --> 00:06:29.889
There's also a lot of trees on site,
which is going to be

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:34.477
creating a lot of shadows.

00:06:34.477 --> 00:06:34.936
By the way,

00:06:34.936 --> 00:06:38.648
guys, this little device helped me through
all the overhead shots in my model.

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:42.193
The Insta360 Link
is an extremely versatile webcam

00:06:42.193 --> 00:06:45.446
because it's got a gamble design
that allows multiple configurations.

00:06:45.446 --> 00:06:49.409
I'm using the overhead mode
to record my model and it records high

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:54.414
quality 4K videos with a half inch sensor
and a really large aperture lens.

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:59.085
It can be easily attached to all standard
arms and it only weighs 100 grams.

00:06:59.085 --> 00:07:02.922
The camera has dedicated software
that allows for a lot of customization,

00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:07.468
including manual focus, manual exposure
and your gimbal movements

00:07:07.468 --> 00:07:08.970
with position presets.

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:11.639
You can also record videos
directly in the app.

00:07:11.639 --> 00:07:12.723
It uses A.I.

00:07:12.723 --> 00:07:14.809
to track your movements
when you move around.

00:07:15.101 --> 00:07:17.562
It can also be controlled
with hand gestures.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:20.940
If you're working in an open environment
like mine, it's got a noise

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:23.943
canceling feature that will get rid
of all of the background noise.

00:07:23.985 --> 00:07:28.489
Check my link in the description
if you want to know more.

00:07:28.489 --> 00:07:33.161
So if we can place the building,
maybe somewhere around here

00:07:33.202 --> 00:07:37.707
on top of the hill, that would be ideal.

00:07:37.707 --> 00:07:41.043
So you can get the nice morning light,

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:46.507
You can get the nice
light from the south during the day

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:48.426
and you can also

00:07:48.426 --> 00:07:51.429
get a nice evening light as well.

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:55.391
And you will get this incredible
view of the hill

00:07:56.517 --> 00:07:59.228
there is that view
into the neighbors house, but

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:01.564
we can probably create
some landscaping around in.

00:08:02.356 --> 00:08:05.443
The other option is to place it
in the middle of the site,

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:08.488
which is closer to the road.

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:10.948
So it's going to be easier
for bringing materials up.

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:12.533
We're not going to have to build

00:08:12.533 --> 00:08:15.369
as long of a driveway,
so it's a little bit more efficient.

00:08:15.703 --> 00:08:19.749
But of course your period of daylight
is a lot shorter because,

00:08:20.041 --> 00:08:28.508
like I said, it's blocked by this hill.

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:32.929
So in order to maximize daylight,
this is roughly 3000 square feet.

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:36.432
Maybe we can have these two volumes
kind of fanned out so that we can

00:08:36.432 --> 00:08:39.644
try to get as much
glazing surface area as possible.

00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:44.023
Or maybe we could do

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:48.736
something like this
so that this top volume

00:08:48.736 --> 00:08:58.621
is getting a little bit
of that southern light.

00:08:58.621 --> 00:09:03.834
And maybe these two volumes are connected
so that this bottom volume borrows

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:08.047
a bit of that light
or we could potentially stack it this way

00:09:09.006 --> 00:09:11.509
so that we have lots of surface

00:09:11.509 --> 00:09:14.554
area facing the morning sun.

00:09:14.554 --> 00:09:16.931
And again,
the top volume gets a little bit

00:09:16.931 --> 00:09:20.560
of that southern light because over here
it's a little bit less steep.

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:24.021
I'm going to just borrow
this tree as a column, but

00:09:24.605 --> 00:09:27.608
maybe we can have
a staggered configuration like this

00:09:27.608 --> 00:09:31.404
so that this area still gets a bit of that

00:09:31.404 --> 00:09:35.616
nice morning light.

00:09:35.616 --> 00:09:39.245
The only problem with placing the building
on top of the hill

00:09:39.245 --> 00:09:43.624
is that you see this line here.

00:09:43.624 --> 00:09:46.877
If you look on the city of over
in the zoning map,

00:09:47.211 --> 00:09:50.590
this area is called the Ridgeway
overlay area.

00:09:51.007 --> 00:09:53.384
I didn't get that. Could you try again?

00:09:53.384 --> 00:09:55.970
And in this area
you can build up to a maximum

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:59.890
of 18 feet in height and 500 square feet.

00:10:01.017 --> 00:10:02.560
The site also

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:07.815
starts to narrow in this direction
and it's also quite a ways up the hill.

00:10:08.024 --> 00:10:12.111
So it might be a little bit
more complicated to bring materials

00:10:12.111 --> 00:10:14.238
or try to build something
all the way up here.

00:10:14.488 --> 00:10:18.284
We're still in the pre design phase,
and so we're not even getting

00:10:18.284 --> 00:10:20.244
into the design part yet.

00:10:20.244 --> 00:10:23.080
And so the point of this exercise
for me, it's

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:26.917
not to identify
exactly where the building is going to go

00:10:27.293 --> 00:10:31.380
because we're still waiting for a survey
and the Geotech report.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:35.176
And honestly,
once we get that, we might find that

00:10:35.176 --> 00:10:37.928
some of these areas
are going to be really hard to build on.

00:10:38.679 --> 00:10:41.891
Maybe the soil is really loose
and we need a lot of fill.

00:10:42.516 --> 00:10:45.311
And so really the point of this

00:10:45.519 --> 00:10:49.940
is for me to try to identify
some of these conditions

00:10:50.232 --> 00:10:52.985
and try to create different scenarios.

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:56.530
So when I do have a conversation
with Geotech and Structural,

00:10:56.739 --> 00:10:59.742
we're not making the decision purely
on structural

00:10:59.742 --> 00:11:02.495
conditions or solar conditions or cost,

00:11:02.953 --> 00:11:06.123
but we are looking at things
a little bit more holistically.

00:11:06.248 --> 00:11:09.794
We can actually talk about the pros
and cons of each option

00:11:09.794 --> 00:11:13.089
in terms of the space
and the experience in the light.

00:11:13.631 --> 00:11:16.175
And I find that when you come

00:11:16.342 --> 00:11:19.720
a little bit more prepared
with your own preferences,

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:24.266
you can have a much more interesting
conversation.

00:11:24.266 --> 00:11:26.686
I presented
some of these ideas to the client

00:11:26.686 --> 00:11:30.856
as well as some different options
for how the building could sit on the site

00:11:31.065 --> 00:11:33.150
would have flowed to what it embed.

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:36.529
Would a cantilever or
or would it be a combination of them?

00:11:37.154 --> 00:11:40.491
Now, as an architect, of course,
you want to start designing and start

00:11:40.491 --> 00:11:42.284
moving into the next phase.

00:11:42.284 --> 00:11:46.122
But as a business owner,
you have to make sure

00:11:46.122 --> 00:11:50.042
that you're not moving into the next phase
until you finish

00:11:50.042 --> 00:11:52.545
one phase and get paid for that phase.

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:56.382
So it's going to be
another couple of weeks until we get

00:11:56.382 --> 00:12:00.344
the survey and the Geotech report,
which is actually perfect

00:12:00.344 --> 00:12:03.973
because during that time
I'm not going to do any work,

00:12:03.973 --> 00:12:13.858
but I can start thinking
about a concept for this building.

00:12:13.858 --> 00:12:16.944
There's something that came up
when I was talking to the client

00:12:17.111 --> 00:12:20.322
and we were having
a really long conversation

00:12:20.322 --> 00:12:24.785
about our vision and what we wanted
to build, and we both agreed.

00:12:24.785 --> 00:12:26.954
We wanted to build
something really unique.

00:12:26.954 --> 00:12:30.166
And he asked a question What is something

00:12:30.166 --> 00:12:33.377
that everyone wants but nobody has?

00:12:33.794 --> 00:12:37.715
I know that's really out there,
but I just want to let you chew on that

00:12:38.507 --> 00:12:42.011
based on what we talked about today
and that question,

00:12:42.428 --> 00:12:46.724
what do you think is the concept
that I'm thinking of in my head?

00:12:47.266 --> 00:13:06.368
Let me know in the comments.

